STEP 4 — CSS tokens (index.css)
-------------------------------
Ground truth discovered: project NEVER defined shadcn semantic tokens. Built dist
CSS had NO .bg-primary / .bg-background / .text-foreground / .text-muted-foreground
/ .border-border (only custom .bg-ink/.text-paper). Existing app works because
call sites pass explicit custom classes that override the no-op shadcn template
defaults via cn()/tailwind-merge. The efferd block requires these tokens, so:
- Added to existing @theme (plain, so vars ARE emitted to :root):
    --chart-1: var(--color-accent);
    --chart-2: var(--color-ink);
    --color-online: var(--color-accent);
    --color-retail: var(--color-ink);
    --color-sales: var(--color-accent);
    --secondary: var(--color-surface);      (legacy bare alias, button.tsx hover)
    --foreground: var(--color-ink);         (legacy bare alias, button.tsx color-mix)
- New @theme inline block with shadcn semantic aliases:
    background -> paper | foreground -> ink | card -> paper | card-foreground -> ink
    primary -> accent | primary-foreground -> paper | secondary -> surface
    secondary-foreground -> ink | muted-foreground -> muted | accent-foreground -> ink
    destructive -> danger | destructive-foreground -> paper | border | input
    ring -> accent | sidebar -> paper | sidebar-foreground -> ink
    sidebar-primary -> accent | sidebar-accent -> accent-soft | sidebar-border | sidebar-ring
- --color-muted deliberately NOT remapped: it is the project's dark-gray TEXT
  token (oklch(0.45 0 0), 42 text-muted usages); shadcn's muted-SURFACE role is
  covered by mapping --color-muted-foreground -> var(--color-muted) instead.
- --card-spacing: self-contained in card.tsx inline ([--card-spacing:--spacing(4)])
  — no action needed.
- Verified in built dist CSS: .bg-background/.text-foreground/.text-muted-foreground/
  .border-border/.divide-border/.bg-card/.bg-primary/.text-primary-foreground/
  .bg-sidebar/.text-sidebar-foreground/.bg-muted/.bg-secondary/.text-destructive/
  .bg-destructive/.border-input ALL PRESENT; runtime vars --chart-1/--chart-2/
  --color-online/--color-retail/--color-sales/--secondary/--foreground/--radius-md/
  --sidebar-width/--sidebar-width-icon/--sidebar-border/--sidebar-accent ALL emitted.
  (--color-background/--color-sidebar absent is EXPECTED: @theme inline inlines
  values into utilities instead of emitting vars, and nothing references them at
  runtime as var().)

