LATENT TYPECHECK BUG FIXED (recorded — collateral of this todo)
---------------------------------------------------------------
- After install, typecheck FAILED in src/lib/__tests__/session.test.ts (7 errors:
  TS2493 at 91/105/116, TS2722 at 93/107/108/118) on
  supabaseAuthMock.onAuthStateChange.mock.calls[0][0].
- Root cause: vi.fn(() => ({...})) with a ZERO-ARG implementation types
  mock.calls as [][] (empty tuples) -> [0][0] is an empty-tuple index error.
  The file was byte-identical to HEAD (06bd0ba) and vitest/tsconfig unchanged —
  the error was LATENT: tsc -b incremental tsbuildinfo skipped a full recheck at
  06bd0ba; the install's npm churn invalidated it, forcing a full recheck.
- Fix: typed the mock's callback parameter per the real supabase-js signature:
    onAuthStateChange: vi.fn(
      (_callback: (event: string, session: unknown) => void) => ({
        data: { subscription: { unsubscribe: vi.fn() } },
      }),
    )
  so mock.calls[0][0] resolves to the callback type. Runtime behavior unchanged;
  all 101 tests still green (session + auth-flow included).

